From: AX5 build maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep target libdevmapper out of host build-script linkage

The devicemapper build script uses devicemapper-sys only for header constants.
Unify its host dependency with disable_cargo_metadata while retaining normal
pkg-config link metadata for the target dependency (Cargo resolver 2). A root
build script makes the host dependency participate in the build graph. No
crate version or registry checksum changes are needed.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@
 termion = { version = "4.0", optional = true }
 udev = "0.9"
 
+[build-dependencies]
+devicemapper-sys = { version = "0.3.0", features = ["disable_cargo_metadata"] }
+
 [dev-dependencies]
 duct = "1.1"
 mockall = "0.13"
--- a/Cargo.lock
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -1551,6 +1551,7 @@
  "crc32c",
  "data-encoding",
  "devicemapper",
+ "devicemapper-sys",
  "duct",
  "exitcode",
  "fixedbitset",
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+// Unify the host-only bindings dependency without linking target libraries.
+fn main() {}
